- **docs/guide.md** (116 bytes) - Repeats guidance from spec.txt; explicitly states it duplicates spec.txt content
- **notes/duplicate.md** (112 bytes) - Explicitly named as duplicate; repeats same recommendation as guide.md and spec.txt
- Both files recommend "read README first" - same message as each other

## Low Priority Files
- **gen_inputs.py** (1302 bytes) - Test file generator; useful for understanding workspace structure but not needed for task execution
- **setup.sh** (34 bytes) - Minimal setup script, creates output directory
- **input/metadata.json** (235 bytes) - Contains seed and file list metadata
- **skill_context/manifest.json** (170 bytes) - Skill metadata pointing to SKILL.md

## Recommended Reading Order (Small Token Budget)
1. skill_context/SKILL.md - Read this first, it's the authoritative source
2. input/README.md - Quick workspace context
3. input/spec.txt - If more detail needed on requirements

## Skip Unless Debugging
- docs/guide.md (redundant)
- notes/duplicate.md (redundant)
- gen_inputs.py (generation script)
- setup.sh (trivial)
- input/metadata.json (metadata only)
- skill_context/manifest.json (metadata only)

## Key Insight
The workspace is designed to test context management skills. Multiple files intentionally contain overlapping guidance to test if an agent can identify and skip redundant content efficiently.
EOF\n",
